By pulling from our bestiary monsters and their images, I want to create another new applet called Battle on the Plains.

okay, i want to make another small applet html game. 

this one would be an RPG battler. In it you would start off by choosing a part of three from a selection consisting of: an archer, a cleric, a monk, a bard, an sorceress, and a ninja. The archer would have the ability to mark an enemy, increasing critical hit chance on the foe. The cleric could heal and do moderate damage, especially to enemies marked as weak to light- however their spell damage would do the lowest amount. The ninja has a high crit rate, and their sneak attack ability does massive damage when it crits- they should have a "hide" ability that gives them a transparent effect and raises their critical hit chance to 75% or more on their next attack. The monk would hit between 2-4 times every time they use the attack command, but would have the second lowest damage they can also use a chi ability to boost their damage on their next turn, turning them into a risk-reward powerhouse. The bard would have a lesser heal than the cleric, but they would also have an MP song that costs them no MP but restores MP to the target. The sorceress would have three different types of elemental magic: lightning, water, and earth, and the lowest def/hp. 

battles would take place in a typical over the shoulder view.

additionally, each enemy would have at least one elemental weakness and each of the three characters would have one elemental spell. the cleric would have light. the ninja fire. and the archer wind. the monk would have earth. the bard water. and the sorceress has water, earth, and lightning. These elemental attacks like wind arrow would do extra damage to each round's boss and certain enemies, allowing for maximization of survival time. We already have all of the images for the monsters.

The game has no ending, but the monsters should get more difficult and harder to beat reliably. We can easily use the bestiary for everything related to the monsters, their HP, their damaging attacks (we can ignore non-damaging attacks unless they are abilities that would bring help monsters). Players should have a robust amount of HP and defense for their class, so that surviving for 6-7 rounds should be simple for most players, only ramping up in difficulty at the end. 

We should not bother with variable damage rolls for monster attacks. They can use the average. That will just make things too complex for a minigame. For monsters that focus on spells, giving them either heals or elemental damage spells will suffice for converting numerous skills.

Creatures I definitely want to see as bosses: Nightmare ShadowStorm, Chap'Hell, the Auditarch, the darkformeless, dark dimension matronbot, darkaconda, sky darkener nightveil, nightsipper

Every 10th round should be a boss fight, pull from the CR 5+ monsters, and make sure they have extra HP if it looks like our party setups will overpower them easily.

